-- title:
--   The coefficient split of the back-substitution sum (round six, `hsplit_of`)
-- statement:
--   **The coefficient split of the back-substitution sum.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegLn5`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.hsplit_of (b : ℕ → ℤ) (W : ℕ) (hsort : L.Pairwise (· < ·)) (r : ℕ) (hr : r < L.length)
--       (hwin : ∀ q, r < q → q < L.length → ¬ bd (L.getD q 0) → S (L.getD r 0) (L.getD q 0) →
--         q ≤ r + W) :
--       bsum P S L A b r = dotF P (cbOf P S L A bd W r) (accZ P S L A b (r + 1)) +
--         dotF P (czOf P S L A bd r) (accB P S L A b (flOf L bd) (r + 1))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Segmented inverse (S2), machine side 5: the coefficient streams of the backward kernel
--
--   For a sorted line `L` and a border predicate `bd` (border positions: the cyclic wrap), the
--   back-substitution sum of row `r` splits into
--
--   * a band part over the next `W` rows (`cbOf W r`, zero on border rows and off the pattern), and
--   * a border part over all later border rows (`czOf r`, against `accB` with flags `flOf`).
--
--   **`hsplit_of`**: the split is exact (the hypothesis of `bwdK_eq`), given the window property
--   `hwin`: a non-border pattern entry `(L_r, L_q)` with `r < q` has `q ≤ r + W`.
--   **`win_of_band`**: for a strictly increasing `L`, a band of half-width `W` in positions gives
--   the window `W` in indices.
